            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0279" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5315/564–565.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Reid to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-10-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 20, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1061.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your cipher cable instruction
                    of October 17 and to my preliminary reply No. 484 of the 18th, I beg now to
                    forward a memorandum communicated to me to-day by Sir Edward Grey in the course
                    of a conversation with him on the subject of the delay in the railway
                    negotiations at Peking.</p>
                <p>Such points of the conversation as are not covered in this memorandum are stated
                    in my cipher cable dispatch sent to-day.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitelaw Reid.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d201-a1.xml" xpointer="d201-a1"/>
            </div>
